# ⚠️ NO ENTRY IN THIS FILE ENDS IN A SLASH, and that is a rule rather than a
# style. A pattern ending in `/` matches a DIRECTORY and nothing else: of the
# four things a path can turn out to be — a directory, a symlink, a file, or
# absent — the trailing form covers exactly one. Every path below is here to be
# hidden whatever it turns out to be, and the paths most likely to be pointed
# somewhere else — a scratch area, a local corpus — are exactly the ones a
# machine shares through a symlink. git treats a symlink as a file, so the
# directory-only form would leave it showing as untracked in this PUBLIC
# repository, one `git add -A` away from a commit.
#
# Dropping the slash costs nothing: it changes matching only for a
# non-directory of the same name, and a component pattern does not reach a
# sibling that merely starts the same way (`render` leaves `render.log` alone).
#
# 🔒 The selftest reads this file (`TY00`) to decide which files a commit would
# carry, with a deliberately small matcher: a bare name, a `/`-anchored path,
# and `*` inside one component. It refuses any other syntax — including a
# trailing slash — rather than guess what it means, so this rule is enforced
# on every run.
node_modules
.DS_Store
# `npm pack` output, from checking what a publish would ship: the scoped name
# packs as rig-c-parts-<version>.tgz, and a checkout of a tag before either
# rename packs under that tag's name.
/rig-c-parts-*.tgz
/rig-parts-*.tgz
/spine-parts-*.tgz
# Local-only areas: session notes, a private corpus link, scratch output. Never
# committed; the corpus is read with `bun run selftest -- --corpus <dir>` and
# never copied here.
/scratch
/corpus
# The heavy half of each public example — painting, See-through inputs and
# layer sets — fetched by `bun run fetch-examples` from the rig-c/examples
# repository at a pinned commit. Anchored, because the selftest's matcher reads
# `*` inside one component and an unanchored pattern with a slash in it would
# never match a single component.
/examples/*/inputs
# Where a sheet or a build lands when run from a checkout without --out.
/render
# Agent worktrees a harness creates inside the checkout while a squad works.
/.claude/worktrees
